  "source": {
    "plan": "Callboard row 2026-11-23 (storyhowto, story-howto, noir), ideas inbox i5, with Canberk's 11-16 note: Milo episode, hook spoken first and big on screen from frame 0, Ghost Light only, about 25s",
    "project": "ppvqmbzuqvzpiuqaiqfy",
    "checked": "2026-11-18: monologue 1120 Orlando (As You Like It, play by William Shakespeare, public_domain), 'Why, how now, Adam?', 76s, overdone 0.30",
    "changed_from_plan": "the board asked for Script, then Cues, then Off book and saying 'line' for a prompt. That is the web's rehearsal; the app (apps/mobile app/run/[id].tsx on main c3665735) has Run it with 'hide the lines': the speech turns to dots and each line comes out as the actor says it. The film shows that and promises nothing else",
    "app": "Ghost Light web preview built from actorrise main apps/mobile (c3665735) plus web-preview.patch, dark theme, demo account, 2026-11-18. app.json on main now lists only ios and android, so the patch adds web to platforms (patch regenerated)",
    "flow": "flows/run-off-book-orlando.json (shots -> public/story/2026-11-23-one-am-off-book/*.png): the speech page, Run it, hide the lines, three lines said through the recorder's scripted mic",
    "voice": "George, one take at stability 0.5, Scribe 0.94 (the spoken 'P O V' and 'one A M' against the written hook); sped up 1.25x with fit_take.py. The say text of line 1 has more words than its text, so the per line word split was redone by hand",
    "new_scene_types": "noir look for StoryVideo (lights off: near black sheet, cream ink, orange); oneam (Milo sitting up in bed, the phone's glow on the ceiling, the clock ticks to 1:01), peeks (he says a line and peeks; pages hop a fence where the sheep should be and a peeks counter climbs), pillow (the pillow over his face, scarf caught on the bedpost, tote tips over, then the arm comes up with the phone)",
    "motifs": "milo-in-bed-1am,phone-glow-on-ceiling,alarm-clock-ticks,peeks-counter-pages-hop-the-fence,pillow-over-face,scarf-caught-on-bedpost,arm-up-with-phone",
